{"kind":"request","text":"J2: a reviewer reads the diff and the interdiff in the AI app\n\nScope: plan 032 section 2b, J2 (notes/plans/032-2026-10-17-journey-as-acceptance-target.md), with the file, diff and interdiff view of notes/2026-10-17-journey-views-design.md. S2 and S6 have landed.\n\nThe scene: a reviewer opens a change in the desktop AI app. An agent has pushed version 2 after the reviewer commented on version 1. The reviewer reads version 2's diff, then reads what changed since version 1, and each view names the exact commits it shows. Over a bound, the view says \"truncated\" and says what it left out.\n\nBuild views of a file at an exact commit, a diff between two exact commits, and an interdiff between two versions of one change. Browser parity is optional. Say in the design section of your note how an interdiff handles a version 2 that was rebased, and what it tells the reviewer when it cannot separate the reviewer's change from the base's.\n\nDone when a reviewer in the desktop AI app reads the diff of version 2 and the interdiff from version 1, on a real room on a deployed Worker, and both name the exact commits they show. Run the real user path for the witness, and name any part that a person must do. A room with a real repository exists on dap-demo.\n\nIf this needs hosted MCP open, or a tool outside the hosted default such as `diff`, name the Worker and the tool in the review request. I open the endpoint in that slice's deploy record, as I did for the hosted agent witness.\n\nOrder: after the failed-claim words and docs. See the act this request's survey rests on for the words items.","body":{"conditions":"A reviewer in the desktop AI app reads the diff of version 2 and the interdiff from version 1 on a deployed Worker, and both name their exact commits, approved by the checker and landed on main.","target_head":"a2501e06c53b4b9743085ea7984a2dae8d65152f","target_ref":"refs/heads/main","target_repo":"git:sha1:589bca982736a2361d15d53f7572375ef2f7aa